3
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:30,040
So using segmentation, a logical address space consists of a collection of segments.

4
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:32,380
So this is different from paging.

5
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:41,320
So for paging, a logical address space basically is a sequence of bytes, one dimensional sequence of bytes.

6
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:46,880
But for segmentation, a logical address space consists of a collection of segments.

7
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,620
So what is a segment?

8
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:53,000
A segment basically is a logical unit of a program.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:04,300
For instance, a segment can be a subroutine, a segment can be a specific data structure used in your program.

10
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,040
