11
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:11,220
So each segment is a sequence of bytes.

12
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:17,540
So different from paging, different segments may have different sizes.

13
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:21,920
So segments can be of variable size.

14
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:32,920
And to do the memory allocation, then we need to do the memory allocation for all the segments in the logic address space.

15
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:39,300
So these segments may not be located contiguously in the physical memory.

16
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:43,300
They can be at different places in the physical memory.

17
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:51,300
So that's why this segmentation scheme is also under the non-contiguous memory allocation category.

